This script starts a Flask web server on port 5000. It listens for HTTP requests on the following endpoints:

- `/version`: Returns the response from the SCPI identification query "*IDN?\n".
- `/getdata`: Returns the current in-memory list.
- `/getset/<int:item_id>`: Returns the item with the given id.
- `/getpost/<int:item_id>/<name>`: Updates the item with the given id or adds a new item.

If an error occurs while communicating with the serial port or while handling the HTTP requests, the server responds with a 503 status code and an error message.

The script also ensures that the serial port is closed when the script is terminated, regardless of whether an error occurred.
